F2 VERDICT: RATIFY WITH CHANGES (5)

---

### Q1. Which of the 23 Dispositions (Section 0) and 3 Rulings (Section 3) Is Wrong?

Five items across the dispositions, rulings, and the inlined repair diff (Section 1b) contain false claims or an invalid settling test (note: we verified by reading [`_scratchpad/w578/jazz_vector_probe.py`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/_scratchpad/w578/jazz_vector_probe.py#L11-L90) and [`ASRUN_NOTE3.txt`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/artifacts/jazzvecdeassert/killtable3_20261102/ASRUN_NOTE3.txt#L8-L25) that items 1–3 below have already been patched in the on-disk probe docstring since [`jazz_vector_probe.ASRUN.py`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/artifacts/jazzvecdeassert/killtable3_20261102/jazz_vector_probe.ASRUN.py#L11-L78) ran):

1. **D3 (and F2 / F3 / F5 / Section 1b contract `:182-183`): "the one CONJUNCTION the real guest exercises, offset 0 read as a byte (`relative_addr == 0 && len == 1`, the inb(PVIS) path)" is FALSE.**
   * **Fact [READ from packet F2/F3 `:57-61`; READ from [`dev_jazz.c`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_jazz.c#L677-L684) and [`jazz_vector_probe.py`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/_scratchpad/w578/jazz_vector_probe.py#L79-L84); REASONED]:**
     `pica_jazzio` (`0xf0000000`, 4 bytes) houses both `PVIS` (offset 0) and `PICA_SYS_LB_IE` (offset 2, 16-bit local-bus interrupt-enable register). As F2 and F3 in the same packet acknowledge, OpenBSD/arc (`picabus.c`) also exercises `out16(PICA_SYS_LB_IE, ...)` (`relative_addr == 2 && len == 2 && writeflag == MEM_WRITE`) in two shapes that are **unrowed** by the 26-row probe:
     * `out16(PICA_SYS_LB_IE, 0)` at `initcpu` (`relative_addr == 2, len == 2, writeflag == MEM_WRITE, idata == 0`): unrowed because `jz ip lbiew` stores `0x0f` (`st16(VEC + 2, 0x0f)`) and `jz ip vecw` stores `0` at offset 0 (`len == 4`).
     * `out16(PICA_SYS_LB_IE, local_int_mask)` at `intr_establish`: unrowed at the UART enable bits because COM0 (`jazz.8`) and COM1 (`jazz.9`) set bits `0x0100` and `0x0200` in `local_int_mask`, whereas `jz ip lbiew` stores `0x0f` (bits 8–15 clear).
   * **On D3's question [REASONED]:** The rule does *not* require rowing every two-input conjunction over driven values of non-tested inputs (which is clause-(e) debt), **Change 1:** drop the false claim that `inb(PVIS)` is the *only* conjunction the real guest exercises, disclose both unrowed `out16(PICA_SYS_LB_IE, ...)` shapes by name in the contract, and file them (`jazzvecrowsowed`).

2. **F1 / F6 (as carried into Section 1b's contract `:175-184` / [`jazz_vector_probe.ASRUN.py`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/artifacts/jazzvecdeassert/killtable3_20261102/jazz_vector_probe.ASRUN.py#L65-L75)): Three overclaims in the repaired contract paragraph:**
   * **(a) "so a re-introduction keyed to `relative_addr` and/or `writeflag` reds" (`:178-179`) is FALSE for `and` [READ from [`dev_jazz.c`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_jazz.c#L666-L694); REASONED]:**
     `relative_addr` on the 4-byte device takes values in `{0, 1, 2, 3}`, while `switch (relative_addr)` merges `1` and `3` into `default:`. Because the probe only reads offset 1 (`ld8(VEC + 1)` at `jz ip dflt`) and only writes offset 3 (`st8(VEC + 3, 0x5a)` at `jz ip dfltw`), `if (relative_addr == 1 && writeflag == MEM_WRITE)` and `if (relative_addr == 3 && writeflag == MEM_READ)` are keyed solely to `relative_addr` and `writeflag` yet score **26/26 green**.
   * **(b) "so a re-introduction keyed to any ONE of them reds" (`:180-182`) is FALSE [READ from [`dev_jazz.c`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_jazz.c#L660-L684) and [`jazz_vector_probe.ASRUN.py`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/artifacts/jazzvecdeassert/killtable3_20261102/jazz_vector_probe.ASRUN.py#L259-L301); REASONED]:**
     `len` (`{1, 2, 4}`), `idata` (`{0, 0x0f, 0x5a}`), and `d->jazz_timer_value` (`{0, 0x0f}`) are multi-valued integers sampled at 2–3 values, not booleans. Single-input predicates that split values *within* a driven side (e.g. `if (idata & 0xff00)`, `if (d->jazz_timer_value & 0xff00)`) or select an undriven value (`if (len == 3)`, `if (idata == 0x5b)`, `if (d->jazz_timer_value == 0x10)`) are keyed to a **single** input and score **26/26 green**. Also in `:181`, "`jazz_timer_value` 0 (rows before lbiew) and 0x0f (rows after)" misplaces `lbiew` itself: `d->jazz_timer_value = idata` ([`dev_jazz.c:681`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_jazz.c#L681)) runs before the tail, so `d->jazz_timer_value` is already `0x0f` on `jz ip lbiew` (confirmed by Table 3's `M_lbnz` redding `lbiew`, 21/26 [READ]).
   * **(c) `(0-7, 10-14: if (!(int_asserted & 0x0300)) ...)` (`:176`) mislabels the example [READ / REASONED]:**
     `0x0300` is `(1 << 8) | (1 << 9)` (the driven pair); `!(int_asserted & 0x0300)` tests the complement of the driven lines, whereas a direct test of undriven lines 0–7, 10–14 is `int_asserted & 0x7cff`.
   * **Change 2:** Narrow the contract wording to single-axis tests / the 6 label-cell keys, qualify single-input kills as holding *at the values the rows drive*, disclose the unrowed default sub-cells `(1, W)` and `(3, R)` and undriven values/bit-ranges as clause-(e) debt, fix "from lbiew on", and distinguish `int_asserted & 0x7cff` from `!(int_asserted & 0x0300)`.

3. **F7 / F21 (as carried into Section 1b's mechanism sentence `:188-190` / [`jazz_vector_probe.ASRUN.py:11-12`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/artifacts/jazzvecdeassert/killtable3_20261102/jazz_vector_probe.ASRUN.py#L11-L12)): "the assert handler raises it when that predicate becomes true" is FALSE (conflates level with edge).**
   * **Fact [READ from [`dev_jazz.c:138-157`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_jazz.c#L138-L157) and [`:451-470`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_jazz.c#L451-L470); REASONED]:**
     Only the `EXT_IMASK` arm (`:466-469`) tests transitions (`!old_assert_3 && new_assert_3`). [`jazz_interrupt_assert()`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_jazz.c#L138-L147) calls `INTERRUPT_ASSERT(d->mips_irq_3)` on **every** call made while `(d->int_asserted & 0x7fff) && (d->int_enable_mask & R4030_EXT_IP3)` holds, even when the predicate was *already* true before the call. That level behaviour is what makes S5's tick healing work (`d->int_asserted` was never cleared by the buggy tail, so the predicate did not "become true" on the healing tick — it was already true).
   * **Change 3:** State in the probe docstring that `jazz_interrupt_assert()` raises on every call made *while* the predicate holds (level, not edge) and `jazz_interrupt_deassert()` lowers on every call made while the predicate is false.

4. **F12 (`:97-100`): "the settling check is `strings` on HEAD's binary against a rebuilt M_b, not run" is WRONG — and the cause is already establishable from the source tree.**
   * **Fact [READ from [`GXEMUL-SEC/src/include/misc.h:181-193`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/include/misc.h#L181-L193), [`GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_jazz.c:696-718`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_jazz.c#L696-L718), and [`GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_sh.c:910-1747`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_sh.c#L910-L1747); REASONED]:**
     In [`misc.h:181-193`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/include/misc.h#L181-L193), `CHECK_ALLOCATION` expands `FAILURE("Out of memory")`, which calls:
     ```c
     snprintf(where_msg, sizeof(where_msg),
         "%s, line %i, function %s().\n",
         __FILE__, __LINE__, __func__);
     ```
     `__LINE__` is passed as an **`int` argument** for `%i`, **not** stringified into `.rodata`! In [`DEVINIT(jazz)`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_jazz.c#L711-L718), `CHECK_ALLOCATION` sits *below* `DEVICE_ACCESS(jazz_jazzio)` (line 712 on HEAD vs line 718 in `M_b` because `M_b` keeps the 7-line `#578` comment plus the 1-line deassert), so the immediate integer operand in `.text` changes from `712` (`0x2c8`) to `718` (`0x2ce`). Meanwhile, in `#577` ([`cpu_sh.c:910-1747`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_sh.c#L910-L1747)), there is **no** `CHECK_ALLOCATION` or `__LINE__` after `sh_exception()` (`:910-918`), which is why `#577`'s `M_b` had HEAD's exact md5!
   * **Change 4:** Correct the F12 record: `strings` cannot see an integer immediate in `.text` and would falsely show no difference; the settling check is `cmp -l` or `objdump -d` on `dev_jazz_init` in `dev_jazz.o` / `gxemul`.

5. **F10 / S4 (`:31-33, :88-93`): Accepting F10 only "as a record" while [`apply_fix578c.py`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/_scratchpad/w578/apply_fix578c.py#L7-L24) writes the SEC-specific comment verbatim into `est/src/devices/dev_jazz.c`.**
   * **Fact [READ from [`apply_fix578c.py:7-24`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/_scratchpad/w578/apply_fix578c.py#L7-L24); REASONED from packet S4/F10]:**
     Per S4 and F10, `est/src/devices/dev_jazz.c` has no `R4030_EXT_IP3` (`EXT_IMASK.IP3`) and keeps `mips_irq_3` equal to `(d->int_asserted & d->int_enable_mask & 0x7fff) != 0`. In `GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_jazz.c` (the tree under review), the shipped comment (1a) is completely true; in `est/src/devices/dev_jazz.c`, the same applier writes `"EXT_IMASK re-enabled IP3"` and `"kept equal to 'a line 0-14 pending and EXT_IMASK.IP3 set'"`, which is false of `est`'s code.
   * **Change 5:** Either note in the F10 record that `est` carries SEC's comment text by applier parity despite using the pre-#69 predicate, or adjust `est`'s comment text to name `est`'s predicate.

*(All other dispositions in Section 0 — F8, F9, F11, F13–F20, F22, F23 — and rulings D1 and D2 hold [READ / REASONED]. On F18, note as a minor completeness point that [`DEVICE_ACCESS(jazz_led)`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_jazz.c#L528-L537) has the same unlatched `default:` `fatal()` shape as `jazz_jazzio`, `jazz_20`, and `jazz_a0` [READ].)*

