### Q3. Is the Shipped Comment (1a) Wrong Anywhere?

* **In [`GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_jazz.c:696-702`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_jazz.c#L696-L702) (the tree under review): NO [READ / REASONED].**
  Every claim in 1a is verified true of `GXEMUL-SEC/src/`:
  1. *"This tail used to deassert the CPU's IRQ3 on every access ("needed by Windows NT during startup"), dropping a level interrupt while JAZZ lines were still pending"*: [`DEVICE_ACCESS(jazz_jazzio)`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_jazz.c#L657-L708) previously ran `INTERRUPT_DEASSERT(d->mips_irq_3)` unconditionally after the `switch` on every read and write without modifying `d->int_asserted` [READ].
  2. *"until a line was asserted anew or EXT_IMASK re-enabled IP3 (OB-22)"*: [`jazz_interrupt_assert()`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_jazz.c#L138-L147) re-asserts `d->mips_irq_3` whenever `(d->int_asserted & 0x7fff) && (d->int_enable_mask & R4030_EXT_IP3)` holds (including from `DEVICE_TICK(ns16550)` at [`dev_ns16550.c:96`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_ns16550.c#L96) and `DEVICE_TICK(jazz)` at [`dev_jazz.c:295, 308`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_jazz.c#L295-L308)); [`jazz_interrupt_deassert()`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_jazz.c#L148-L157) never asserts; and [`case R4030_SYS_EXT_IMASK:`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_jazz.c#L451-L470) asserts `d->mips_irq_3` iff `!old_assert_3 && new_assert_3`, which with `d->int_asserted & 0x7fff` already nonzero requires `EXT_IMASK.IP3` to transition `0 -> 1` ("re-enabled IP3") [READ / REASONED].
  3. *"The CPU line is kept equal to 'a line 0-14 pending and EXT_IMASK.IP3 set' by jazz_interrupt_assert()/_deassert() and the EXT_IMASK arm; an access to this register no longer touches it"*: Those three sites ([`:144`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_jazz.c#L144), [`:154`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_jazz.c#L154), [`:467-469`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_jazz.c#L467-L469)) are the sole writers of `d->mips_irq_3` (`mtc0 Cause` at [`cpu_mips_coproc.c:949-954`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_mips_coproc.c#L949-L954) writes IP0/IP1 only), and `DEVICE_ACCESS(jazz_jazzio)` no longer touches `d->mips_irq_3` [READ / REASONED].
* *(Note on `est` per S4/F10: as stated in Q1 Change 5, in `est/src/devices/dev_jazz.c` the `EXT_IMASK.IP3` wording is not true of `est`'s pre-#69 code [READ].)*

